  texts:
  - The village is burning. The great bell has stopped.
  - Mira...? Mira! Where are you?
  - The lantern is warm in his hands. Something tall and dark rises out of his shadow.
  - Stay away from me! ...Why won't it hurt me?
  - An ember beast. Shoot it with the lantern (J). Hold J to charge a stronger flare.
  - A burning enemy glows cyan for a moment. Press P and Mira's shadow strike finishes
    it.
  - The path is broken. The burning gap is far too wide to jump.
  - Shoot the cracked tree three times (J). It will fall across the gap and become
    your path.
  - 'A memory: Mira kneels, closing his small hands around the lantern.'
  - If the bell ever stops, carry the light to the clock tower. Promise me.
  - ...I promised.
  - Ember beasts crawl out of the ash of the square.
  - There are so many... I can't go back.
  - Light them up, little brother. I'll do the rest.
  - That voice... no. It can't be.
  - The forest. She said the lantern always knows the way to the tower.
  - Behind him, the shadow lowers one long hand between the boy and the flames.
  - The Dark Forest. The fire never reached it. Only the shadows did.
  - You followed me. You always follow me.
  - Someone has to keep you out of trouble.
  - ...Mira? Is it really you?
  - The shadow does not answer. The fireflies drift closer.
  - Hollow shapes rise out of the black earth.
  - They look like they're made of my own shadow.
  - Fire shows them. I finish them. Together, Ilyan.
  - 'Another memory: dry cloth in the storeroom. The lantern slipping from his fingers.'
  - The flame spreading faster than he could scream.
  - I dropped it. It was me. It was always me.
  - I know. I came back for you anyway.
  - The black water is too wide, even for a double jump.
  - Shoot the cracked dead tree three times (J). It will fall and become your bridge.
  - In the clearing something old is waiting. A blade made for endings.
  - You dropped the lantern, boy. You remember. You always remember.
  - ...It was an accident.
  - Tell that to the fire.
  - Don't listen to it. Stay behind me, Ilyan. Not this time.
  - The tower. The clock stopped at one minute to midnight... the minute I dropped
    it.
  - Then let's go and see what is waiting at the top.
  - The Clock Tower. Every gear inside is frozen at 11:59.
  - If I turn the clock back... maybe none of it ever happened.
  - Time doesn't forgive, Ilyan. But it remembers.
  - The tower lends him a little of its power. Hold Q, and the last moments run backwards.
  - The tower's crushers slam on the beat of the clock.
  - Wait for the red glow to fade as it rises, then run under it. Caught? Hold Q
    to rewind.
  - At the top of the tower, the clockwork opens one great eye.
  - It's watching me. It has been watching all night.
  - Every second you replay. Every second you regret.
  - Then we will give it something new to watch.
  - Far below, something heavy and horned begins to climb.
